  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Quiet weather through the upcoming week. Isolated shower\nchances will persist for areas along and north of the I-64\ncorridor from the Nor'easter and its wrap around moisture. \n\n\nThe Nor'easter off the Mid-Atlantic coast looks to push slightly\nsouthwest through Sunday. As this happens, some wrap around\nmoisture and cloud cover may move into the area, especially for\nareas along and north of I-64. Overall, the impacts from this\nsystem will remain minimal for the region. Gusty northwest winds\nwill continue to remain in the 15-25 mph range through Sunday\nafternoon, with diminishing winds through Sunday night into\nMonday morning expected. \n\nBy Tuesday, the Nor'easter and its associated upper level trough\nfinally lift north and east of the region, which will allow for\n500mb heights and upper level ridging to build back into the\nregion. This will return daytime highs back into the upper 70s\nto low 80s for mountain locations, and upper 80s to low 90s for\nPiedmont locations starting Wednesday and continuing through the\nend of the work week. While temperatures will surge to above\nnormal values again, dewpoints look to remain in the 40s/50s\nwhich will make the airmass feel much more tolerable. \n\nA possible frontal passage late on Friday looks to moderate \ntemperatures back to near normal to start the weekend, and\nreturn widespread rainfall to the area.",
